.TH flightlog-export 1 2026-09-30 "flightlog 0.3.0" "flightlog manual"
.SH NAME
flightlog\-export \- Export a session to a redacted .flightlog.zip
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBflightlog export\fR [\fB\-\-no\-redact\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-path\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-size\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-tool\fR] [\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-checksums\fR] [\fB\-\-input\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-format\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-cwd\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-content\-checks\fR] [\fB\-\-overwrite\fR] [\fB\-\-summary\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-http\fR] [\fB\-\-goal\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-unredacted\fR] [\fB\-\-state\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-yolo\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-native\fR] [\fB\-\-redact\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-reviewed\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-metadata\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Export a session to a redacted .flightlog.zip.
.PP
Picks the newest session recorded for the directory (any tool) unless \-\-tool or \-\-session say otherwise. Prints the redaction report, then the file\*(Aqs size and SHA\-256. Review the report before sharing the bundle.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-redact\fR
Preserve sensitive content for private migration (bundle is not encrypted)
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-path\-checks\fR
Allow traversal, absolute destinations and filesystem symlinks
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-size\-checks\fR
Disable Flightlog archive, entry and input size limits
.TP
\fB\-\-tool\fR \fI<TOOL>\fR
Tool the session belongs to [default: whichever has the newest session]
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
claude: Claude Code
.IP \(bu 2
codex: OpenAI Codex CLI
.IP \(bu 2
opencode: opencode
.IP \(bu 2
gemini: Gemini CLI
.IP \(bu 2
cursor: Cursor CLI (cursor\-agent) and the Cursor editor
.IP \(bu 2
copilot\-vscode: GitHub Copilot chat in VS Code and compatible editors
.IP \(bu 2
copilot: GitHub Copilot CLI
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Session id [default: the newest session for the directory]
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-checksums\fR
Ignore manifest SHA\-256 mismatches (ZIP decoding must still succeed)
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read a Copilot CLI event log or VS Code chat file (requires \-\-tool copilot or copilot\-vscode)
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-format\-checks\fR
Skip bundle schema and file\-inventory validation
.TP
\fB\-\-cwd\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory the session ran in [default: current directory]
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-content\-checks\fR
Skip input redaction and opaque\-content checks, regardless of manifest mode
.TP
\fB\-\-overwrite\fR
Replace existing outputs and restore files; merge extraction directories
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-http\fR
Permit plaintext HTTP transfers
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-unredacted\fR
Accept explicitly unredacted bundles for private migration
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Output file [default: <session>.flightlog.zip]
.TP
\fB\-\-yolo\fR
Disable redaction and every bypassable safety check; overwrite outputs
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-native\fR
Leave out native files; shared history can still be converted with restore \-\-to TOOL
.TP
\fB\-\-redact\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
File of private literal names/domains to redact (one per line; kept local)
.TP
\fB\-\-reviewed\fR
Record in the bundle that a person reviewed the redaction report
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-metadata\fR
Include working directory and Git metadata (may identify private projects)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUMMARY
.TP
\fB\-\-summary\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Summary as JSON: {goal, state, decisions, open_questions, next_steps, files_touched}
.TP
\fB\-\-goal\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
What the session set out to do (instead of \-\-summary)
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Where it stands now (instead of \-\-summary)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  flightlog export \-\-goal \*(AqMigrate auth to OIDC\*(Aq \-\-state \*(AqLogin works; logout TODO\*(Aq
  flightlog export \-\-summary summary.json \-\-reviewed \-o handoff.flightlog.zip
  flightlog export \-\-tool codex \-\-session <id> \-\-no\-native
.TP
.B COPILOT_HOME
Copilot CLI configuration and state directory (default ~/.copilot).
.TP
.B COPILOT_VSCODE_USER_DATA_DIR
VS Code compatible editor user data root (the directory containing User).
By default, Code, Code Insiders and VSCodium user data locations are searched.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flightlog (1)
